From d0797e289bc08d74d3b8542d7215c9623b5f3788 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 07:33:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): route origin chat comments to their bound owner
 [daveey]

The owner decision notice already reaches remote origin chats, but their
kanban_comment tool still refused replica-only targets. Add a comment-only
courier route scoped to a validated, unreleased local origin binding and the
current chat's continuation. Unrelated chats and workers keep their existing
paths; this grants no unblock or human-answer authority.

Reuse one durable transport request for identical text on the same owner ask.
Distinguish queued/unknown and unconfirmed outcomes from owner-confirmed
application. Reject oversized payloads before the legacy courier can truncate.

Proof: 18 new tests, existing origin-decision and notice regressions; removing
the tool route produces two failing tool-entry tests. scripts/check passes.
The transport boundary is simulated; owner-side add_comment and gateway-aware
comment probe are real SQLite operations, not a fabricated success receipt.

Hermes-Card: t_7bdfdcdd4ec572a5
